@brief Sanitize a file name or full file path for safe cross-platform / cloud / web use.
@param _filePath: the raw file name or path (UTF-8). The input is auto-detected as a standalone
file name or a full path (it is a path when it contains a slash or a drive letter such as
"C:"). Processing per component: NFC Unicode normalization; stripping of characters that
conflict with Windows / cloud clients / HTTP-FTP
(< > : " | ? * # % & { } \ $ ! ' @ + = and ASCII control characters); spaces become '_';
leading/trailing spaces and periods are trimmed; "." and ".." segments are dropped; Windows
reserved device names (CON, PRN, AUX, NUL, COM1..9, LPT1..9) get a trailing '_' on the stem;
each component is truncated to 255 bytes on a UTF-8 boundary. Drive letters (e.g. "C:") and
UNC / POSIX roots are preserved, and mixed slashes are collapsed.
@return a CleanedPathResult holding the path in universal ('/'), Windows native ('\') and Windows
long-path (\\?\ / \\?\UNC\) forms, plus the isolated and percent-encoded file name.
"""

